@@ -77,6 +77,10 @@ Exit codes: `0` finished or stopped normally, `2` needs a human, `3` blocked but
 | `CARCODE_MANAGER_PUSH` | unset = **off** | Unset or `0`: never push; verified commits stay local. `1`: push verified work to `origin` under the same branch name, never forced, only for non-protected automation branches. Any other value is an error. The launcher's `-AllowPush` switch enables it for one run. `main` and protected branches are never pushed. |
 | `CARCODE_MANAGER_STATE_DIR` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\CarCodeAI\agent-manager` | Runtime state and logs. Refused if inside the repository. |
 | `CARCODE_CLAUDE_BIN` | auto | Path to `claude.exe`. |
+| `CARCODE_CANONICAL_REPO` | unset | The canonical CarCode checkout. When set, the manager refuses any checkout that is neither it nor one of its linked worktrees (an independent copy or clone), so a duplicate folder is never managed as CarCode. Set it once, at user level. |
+
+Every run logs which workspace it uses, and `-Status` shows it: the canonical repository, and the linked
+worktree when a task runs in one. Saved state stays per worktree, because a task belongs to one branch and tree.
 
